<Defs>
	<BiomeDef>
		<defName>RP_ColdDesert</defName>
		<label>cold desert</label>
		<description>Cold deserts are arid regions where low temperatures combine with minimal precipitation to create harsh, barren landscapes. Unlike hot deserts, these areas experience freezing winters and cool summers. Vegetation is extremely sparse, limited to hardy shrubs and grasses that can survive both aridity and cold. The rocky, windswept terrain offers little shelter, and water is scarce year-round. Despite the challenges, some specialized wildlife has adapted to these extreme conditions.</description>
